## Goal

The open deck in `/decks` gets Undo and Redo. Each add, removal, rename and cosmetic change (portrait, playmat, backdrop, card back) is one step. Undo sends the step's old values and Redo its new ones through `store.updateDeck`, so each is an ordinary edit that saves and syncs (R256). Ctrl/Cmd+Z undoes and Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z redoes, except in a text field. A new edit after an Undo empties Redo. The history starts empty whenever the open deck changes (another deck, a trio, an import, nothing) and goes when the workshop unmounts. Both buttons are disabled when there is nothing to move, and Vitest covers each of these.

